                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Ok, so indeed like 'indent-blankline.nvim', but for actually present indents. At the moment this can't be done and I don't have plans to implement it in the near future. 'mini.indentscope' can somewhat work alongside 'indent-blankline.nvim', though, and I want to make it work seamlessly (not possible with current Neovim functionality).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Ok, so indeed like 'indent-blankline.nvim', but for actually present indents. At the moment this can't be done and I don't have plans to implement it in the near future. 'mini.indentscope' can somewhat work alongside 'indent-blankline.nvim', though, and I want to make it work seamlessly (not possible with current Neovim functionality).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Ok, so indeed like 'indent-blankline.nvim', but for actually present indents. At the moment this can't be done and I don't have plans to implement it in the near future. 'mini.indentscope' can somewhat work alongside 'indent-blankline.nvim', though, and I want to make it work seamlessly (not possible with current Neovim functionality).",
